Targets: reader-narrow removes private-kind admission; reader-broad accepts unrelated internal kinds; human-fence removes the original durable-human guard; pending/approval/artifact/completed remove their respective exact guards; catalog-cas removes the approval compare-and-swap leg; run-cas takes a late version instead of the captured version; decode removes final self-readability; goal removes unbound-goal propagation; trigger removes automatic queuing; recovery-order queues before releasing a held completed reservation; external-admin changes the process-local family entries from ADMIN to GOAL.

After all drills, all three targeted live source hashes matched their predrill values exactly (criterion-run.ts, criterion-runner.ts, daemon-command-vocabulary.ts). The temporary config was removed via its literal owned path, with no source restoration operation. The real six-file45-test criterion suite then passed EXIT0, followed by daemon typecheck EXIT0. This proves the exercised guards are load-bearing without exposing any peer gate to physical source mutation.
